<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agha Mohammad Khan Qajar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1742">1742</a>–<a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agha Mohammad Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> was the founder of the Qajar dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in the late eighteenth century. He defeated the last Zand rulers and reunited Iran under Qajar rule. In 1796 he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mashhad">Mashhad</a> from the last Afsharid ruler, Shahrokh, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>'s remnant state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agha-mohammad-khan-qajar.jpg" alt="Agha Mohammad Khan Qajar" width="289" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sotheby's · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_portrait_of_Agha_Muhammad_Khan,_Persia,_Qajar,_dated_1795.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
